      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, this is much more useful. the physical separation and color-coding make sense. \n\none thing that's still bothering me, though, is when things go completely sideways. even with all these rules, there are always those tiny, almost invisible errors—like a single drop of oil from a different pan making it into a vegan sauce, or someone using a slightly dirty knife by mistake. it feels like these little issues just \"appear\" out of nowhere in the middle of a rush. \n\ncan you give me some advice on managing those specific, unpredictable little errors? how do I train staff to be hyper-aware of those tiny, almost \"sneaky\" ways contamination can happen during the chaos of a live service?",
